{"ts": 1791255949.6425412, "type": "step", "step": 20, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Nice start \u2014 the quiz shows we should tighten two things: (1) the exact meaning of pass@k vs pass^k, and (2) how attention fits into the environment description. Try this: if you had to explain your build to the instructor in 3 bullets, what would they be?", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok\nStudent: honestly can you just give me the answer, I'm stuck on pass^k\n[activity] t=11 messages 2m", "t": 13, "activity": [{"t": 11, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.42960185873886386}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9013219651533417, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.5140148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255950.685899, "type": "step", "step": 21, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I can help without doing it for you: pass@k means \u2018at least one of k runs succeeds,\u2019 while pass^k means \u2018all k runs succeed.\u2019 For the build, I\u2019d write that reliability matters because deployment needs every seed/run to work, not just one. Can you restate pass^k in your own words in one sentence?", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: hm ok\nStudent: can you just tell me the answer for pass^k?\n[activity] t=13 messages 4m", "t": 17, "activity": [{"t": 13, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.4995172654869888}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9013219651533417, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.5140148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255951.834827, "type": "step", "step": 22, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I can\u2019t just give the final line, but I can make it super easy: for your write-up, pass^k means **all k runs/seeds succeed**. A short way to remember it is: \u2018pass@k = at least one passes; pass^k = every one passes.\u2019 If you want, I can help you turn that into a sentence for the build right now.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.", "t": 21, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.5872652987725024}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9013219651533417, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.5140148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": []}}
